News - How to deal with the problem of RV battery power consumption
How to deal with the problem of RV battery power consumption
First of all, we need to know the approximate power consumption of the commonly used appliances in the RV in a day.
A 90-liter refrigerator can be used throughout the day, and the cumulative power consumption will not exceed 0.5 degrees. (Generally, it is recommended to use an intermittent stop, so that the starting time of the refrigerator can be controlled, and it will not exceed 0.2 degrees in a day)
A 100-watt notebook (generally 60 watts) is expected to use 5 hours a day, and the cumulative power consumption is 500 watts, which is about 0.5 kWh.
An electric rice cooker of about 800 watts, with a volume of 4L, is expected to be used twice a day for a total of half an hour, and the cumulative power consumption is 400 watts, which is about 0.4 kWh.
6.An 800-watt electric hot water bottle with a volume of 4 liters. It is expected to be used 3 times a day, each time for 5 minutes, and the cumulative power consumption is 200 watts, which is about 0.2 kilowatt-hours of electricity.
9.Calculated by a horse of air conditioner, it is about 1000 watts for an hour, so if it is turned on for 5 hours, it will consume 5 kWh of electricity.
