Know the meaning of decimal numbers
In this case, Bruna spent R $ 7,00. The number of decimal places remains the same.
Now we are going to know another example of situations that we live in our daily life where we can apply, this time, the multiplication of decimal by decimal:
The sum of the number of decimal places of the two numbers that were multiplied determines the number of decimal places in the answer, and in cases where zero is the last number of the decimal part, it is not taken into account, leaving the total value of the Henrique bought the value of R € 11,70.
As long as we multiply a decimal number by a natural number, the decimal places in the answer are the same as the number that was multiplied. In the case of multiplying decimal by decimal, the decimal places in the answer are the sum of the decimal places of the two numbers that were multiplied.
