Greater than: How to differentiate this symbol from others?
Perhaps, you have wondered what is the meaning of "greater than", And how to differentiate it from other mathematical symbols. Well, not knowing how to recognize it, is something quite normal until we become familiar with them.
To which side should I place the greater than symbol?
In this case, two emblems called: greater than symbol (>), and less than symbol (<). Each one has a representation in the shape of an arrow or a rotated V, highlighting the largest opening towards the largest number, always located on the left side.
When we come across some numbers, we can easily identify which is the greatest and which is the least. For example: We have these numbers and we must find the largest and the smallest: 1,3 and 5.
It is common for schools to have some confusion at the time of writing, but nothing that practice does not solve it. If there is difficulty with these symbols, calligraphy lessons or practice between different figures can be done.
To avoid confusion at the time of writing, it should be remembered that if the opening points to the right side (in the same way it will show the greater than), but in this case, the general emblem of the exercise will represent the less than.
We can see that the greater than symbol, has the large opening towards the quantity that is greater than the other quantity, marking the difference between them. This is called an inequality sign (because both quantities are NOT equal.
To make it much easier for you to remember the symbols, you may notice that the side that indicates the amount less than is much smaller. This way you will be able to quickly differentiate the signs when you find yourself with greater or lesser amounts.
Not only did he leave a great legacy in the area of optics and refraction of light on different surfaces, but he also managed to create different ways of symbolizing a wide variety of mathematical representations. Which undoubtedly help us a lot today.
1.000 is greater. Now you must write it with the correct sign.
It is followed by 345 and finally, the smallest is 250. Then we proceed to write them with the sign greater than:
(20 is less than 21). Note: Remember that you must learn to read the quantities, it is essential so that you know how to differentiate the figures correctly, you have to memorize the major sign of the minor, and finally, it is important that you put why both quantities are unequal, in this In this case, you just have to write the quantities and define the corresponding sign.
