There is told the story of a father who has two children of which the child decides to ask what corresponds to his inheritance.
When he has nothing left, his supposed friends leave him alone, he finds himself in the street without knowing what to do.
Upon arriving in front of his father the young man is greeted with joy, the man decides to have a party because his son had returned. The young man's clothes were changed and he was given a new ring.
This is one of the most popular stories we find in the sacred scriptures and leaves us important teachings such as repentance and the love that the Father has for us.
Repentance after losing everything
The prodigal son: Attitude makes a difference ...
Many times we think that this is about a capricious child who asked for all his money and, after having spent everything, decides to return, but in yes the story is much deeper that this and leaves us lessons that can be of much benefit to our lives.
Just like the prodigal son, God gives us life and everything we have to live it to the fullest and we waste it by dedicating it to doing other things and, in the worst case, to doing evil, harming our neighbors and others. behaviors that are not good for us.
It does not mean that we will be perfect, but that we will try to comply with the will of God and we will live near the Father.
This is one of the teachings that this parable leaves us; If we repent, we will find the Father's forgiveness.
This is an interesting teaching because many times we think that what we have done does not deserve forgiveness from God.
The word of God emphasizes in several passages, that when a sinner repents in heaven there is a party, that the love that the Father has for us is greater than anything bad we have done.
As the prodigal son did, he realized that in his father's house he had everything he needed and this is not about money but about feeling protected, loved and, above all, accepted.
Being able to recognize our faults and ask for forgiveness for our sins is important but more valuable is when we are genuinely sorry.
When we breathe when we can do some activity, when we see nature, it shows the father's love for his children and only those who truly repent can call themselves children of God, while we do not do it, we are simply God's creation.
In this story we see three attitudes that we must take into account and we will detail them one by one in order to be able to extract all the learning that can be done.
This is a single father who had raised his two children with the same benefits for each. A family of good standing that already has two children at a stage where they can make their own decisions.
The father was understood and pacifying, he knew how to accept his son's request and respect it even though it hurt. He was just because he delivered what he asked for in full, without taking anything away.
At first we see a proud son, who only seeks his own benefit. That he seems not to care about his father's feelings and that he decides to move away to enjoy life with the company of those friends who left him when he saw himself with nothing.
He also received his inheritance, the same amount that was given to his brother. However he decided to stay.
The three attitudes let us learn a lot. If we are parents what we want is to see our children happy and for this, sometimes, we must say no.
Fill us with mercy towards our neighbor and show more empathy at all times.
