Powerful prayers to achieve grace and fulfill your deepest desires
"Also the kingdom of heaven is similar to a merchant looking for good pearls."
With this parable, Jesus wanted his disciples to learn the value and importance of the Kingdom of Heaven by comparing it with the most precious pearl that that merchant could get.
The story revolves around a person who was dedicated to the trade, purchase and sale of items, more specifically, pearls. Through this parable, Jesus achieved his goal and make both his disciples, as well as the other people who listened to him, understand what he wanted to teach with the pearl of great price.
After a long time and a long journey, searching and acquiring the best pearls; the merchant, manages to find a stone of these without equal. This does not mean that the merchant's journey has ended, because now he must have acquired it in some possible way; he, for his part, was willing to give anything to acquire this pearl, since it was one of a kind.
A great exchange for the pearl of great price
Despite this, the merchant did not want to miss this opportunity (besides it could be unrepeatable); So, one of the ways that he came up with to be able to acquire that pearl was to sell everything he owned. Although it seemed a rather risky bet, he already had total determination with what he wanted and knew, that acquiring that pearl, he could not get it anywhere else, and never again in his life.
The way of Jesus, his way of life, his teachings, his gospel; it is something truly incalculable and invaluable, that perhaps it is possible to achieve only once in a lifetime. The Kingdom of Heaven, which would be the pearl, for us to access it, requires a great price; It will be up to us whether or not we decide to give something of great value as well.
Finally, the parable also teaches us that, if we try hard to get what we want so much; Sooner or later, all our efforts and sacrifices may be rewarded. If you live a life in God, in Jesus, you will never have to sit idly by and wait for things to happen alone.
One of the most common (and precious) ways that Jesus used to teach certain lessons to his disciples and followers; It was through parables and stories, these stories contain within themselves an extremely enormous moral and spiritual background. Jesus used them to illustrate his teachings and although he gave explanations of it, many could be left to the free thought of each person.
As well as the pearl of great priceWe can also find parables in the bible such as "The Good Samaritan", "The lost sheep", "The sower", "The prodigal son" and many more; of which, we will be able to obtain other teachings that will help us throughout our lives.
In the following video that we leave you below, you can find a reflection on this beautiful fable. Remember, that your interpretation is also valid and acceptable.
