Rosary for the Dead: Mysteries, promises and much more
Know through this article, the details about the rosary for deceased, a ritual carried out at wakes and novenaries, to ask for deceased relatives and that they be given eternal rest and perpetual light. Do not miss the information that we will show you here.
Some of the promises of the Virgin Mary to those who pray the rosary
El rosary for deceased, Also called Holy Rosary of the Dead, is a ritual carried out after the wake and burial of a loved one, and it is quite important for Christians, since, in this ritual, they ask for the forgiveness of the deceased's soul, so that he can rest in peace eternally .
Now, the Holy Rosary for the dead can be done on any day of the week, and each of these days corresponds to a Mystery, which forms a group called "Mysteries for the deceased". These mysteries are made up of 4 series, which in turn consist of 5 mysteries for each series.
These mysteries narrate the incarnation of the Son of God; the birth and childhood of the Child Jesus. These mysteries are prayed on Monday and Saturday of each week.
Visit: recounts Mary's visit to Elizabeth, who upon hearing Mary's greeting, the child in her womb jumped for joy; Elizabeth, filled with the Holy Spirit, tells Mary "Blessed are you among all women and blessed is the fruit of your womb."
Presentation of the Son of God in the temple: it relates when, at 8 days old, the Child Jesus was circumcised and presented in the temple as the Law of the Lord says, in Jerusalem.
If you found this post interesting, we invite you to read our article on:Novena to the Virgen del Carmen for every day.
The mysteries of light in the Holy Rosary for the dead They narrate the public life of Jesus of Nazareth, ranging from the baptism of Jesus to the eve of his Passion. These mysteries correspond to Thursdays of each week.
The wedding at Cana: This story talks about the first miraculous sign of Jesus, who, at a wedding in Cana, at the request of his mother Mary, turned the wedding water into Wine.
The transfiguration: the mystery tells of the transfiguration of Jesus in front of Peter, James and John, showing them his divine grace.
Prayer in the Garden: the mystery counts when, together with his disciples, Jesus prayed in anguish "My Father, if possible, let this cup pass from me, but not as I want, but as you want."
Crowning with thorns: tells how Pilate's soldiers undressed Jesus, placing a purple robe over him and putting a crown of thorns on his head, while making fun of him.
The crucifixion: narrates the moment of the crucifixion, shouting with his last breath "Father, in your hands I put my spirit! ".
The glory mysteries of rosary for deceased they correspond to the stories about the resurrection of Jesus Christ. These mysteries are meditated on on Wednesdays and Sundays.
Rise of JesusAfter his resurrection, Jesus, who was not resurrected in human form, did so to make it clear that men and women must focus their lives on the fulfillment of the Word and its commandments, in order to enter the kingdom of heaven.
Ascension of Mary: in the fourth mystery the rise of Mary to the kingdom of heaven is related, after angels sent by God the Father to her, and Mary ascends to the kingdom of heaven by means of a trail of light that came from an opening in heaven.
In life and death, all those who pray my rosary will have the light and fullness of my grace.
All those who pray my rosary are my beloved children, and they are also the brothers of my son Jesus.
