In mathematics, we see the concept of a fraction: a part of a whole that can be represented geometrically or numerically.
In this way, equivalent fractions are those written in different ways, but that represent the same part of a whole. For example, the following fractions are equivalent.
To find equivalent fractions, we must multiply the numerator and denominator by the same natural, nonzero number.
Equivalent fractions have a different number representation, but they express the same amount.
For that, we only need to apply the principles of simplifying fractions. But what would that be?
Note that when they are reduced as much as possible (irreducible way), the fractions become identical and therefore they are equivalent.
It is important to remember that in fractions, the top term is called the numerator while the bottom term is called the denominator.
When multiplying fractions, simply multiply one numerator by the other and then one denominator by the other.
Multiplication is done this way, regardless of the number of fractions.
The numerator of the first fraction multiplies the denominator of the second;
The numerator of the first fraction multiplies the denominator of the second and the remaining fractions;
The denominator of the first fraction multiplies the numerator of all other fractions.
Prayer to Saint Martin of Porres, is a powerful weapon in the hands of people who maintain a strong and healthy faith. The prayer San Martin de Porres It represents salvation in many medical cases and involving people of color.
San Martín de Porres is a very popular saint in South America due to the many miracles attributed to him long before his beatification.
When he was not accepted by his paternal family, he was left in the custody of Mrs. Isabel García, who lived in San Lázaro, in a town inhabited by people of color.
He began his religious preparation in the Dominican convent Our Lady of the Rosary but he was very rejected due to the mulatto tone of his skin color.
His gift for healing was seen in humans and animals, all the patients Martin treated received healing, in many cases, immediately.
It is said that, apart from the gift of healing, some others were granted to him, such as the gift of tongues and even the gift of flying.
