The gifts of the Holy Spirit: Gifts of Inspiration
This particular gift, when manifested, does not reveal future events but rather of the past or present that are in the occult.
The gift of spirit discernment
The Apostle Paul shows us a clear manifestation of this gift when he was able to discern the spirit that operated in Elimas, that passage is found in the book of the Acts of the Apostles in chapter 13 verses 9 and 10.
It is one of the most amazing gifts because when it manifests it is done through supernatural miracles, with things that, humanly speaking, are impossible.
Gift of faith
In the word of God he tells us about a man who says he was full of power and grace, that is, the gift of faith was manifested in him, this man is Stephen and his story is in the book of Acts of the Apostles in chapter 6 from verse 8 onwards. Gift of Health
In this gift the plural is used because there are several gifts of healing and not just one as in the others. In other words, a person can have the manifestation of some gift of healing, so it does not manifest itself by healing all diseases but some.
This gift can be used to exhort, edify, comfort, teach, and convince. It is a gift that must be used with responsibility and order because it is speaking in the name of God.
Speaking in tongues is a manifestation of the Holy Spirit, but when this happens, only one genre of language is spoken.
When this gift is manifested use the body of the believer but everything is dominated only by the mind of Christ.
This gift, as is the last one, begins to be seen when the dispensation of grace begins, which is the period in which we still live. This gift is manifested to give meaning to the various languages that can be spoken when the Holy Spirit takes control of the Church.
The gifts of the Holy Spirit are given for divine purposes and must be manifested in order so that they can fulfill their purpose without interruption.
