Pope Benedict XIV, in the year 1742, was the one who granted plenary absolution to the medal of Saint Benedict of Nursia, provided that its carrier meets the following conditions:
Help the poor and the sick.
If a person says a prayer before Holy Mass or before receiving Communion, he receives 100 days of indulgence.
Everyone who celebrates as a minister or is present at Holy Mass, as well as those who pray for their Christian brothers and their leaders, will have 7 years of indulgence.
Anyone who prays for the works of the Benedictine Order may receive the grace of a portion of all the good works that the said Order performs.
