It seems thatat the very moment of his conversion the demon in the form of a raven appeared to himwith the intention of dissuading him, yelling at him"Cras, cras, cras",whose meaning in Latin is "tomorrow, tomorrow, tomorrow."
"I will not leave anything for tomorrow, from today I will be a Christian ”, He snapped. Such firm expression has earned him the title of saint who attends to urgent problems.
Who is the saint who meets the most pressing needs?
Story created around the soldier of the Roman legion "Fulminante"
Some sources place him as a contemporary of Saint Philomena and affirm that his martyrdom took place on April 19, 303. Although he is a saint recognized by the Catholic faithful, he does not appear in the Catholic liturgy.
Did the saint whose name means "fast" really exist?
These relics would have been unearthed from the catacombs of the plazaDenfert-Rochereau. The fact that the sender, belonging to the same city, wrote the word"Spedito"(which is translated by “express mail”), with the intention of speeding up its delivery, made the nuns think that the relics belonged to someone called “San Spedito”.
It was not long before it was assigned a date, corresponding to the fourth century, with the aim of giving it plausibility. It's considered"Lawyer of impossible causes"a title that he shares with Santa Rita and with San Judas Tadeo.
The truth is that from the end of the XNUMXth century and even perhaps from before, a story was generated about this mysterious saint.
This legion was composed mainly of Christian soldiers, whose main mission was the defense of the eastern borders of the territories that the Romans invaded against the attacks of the Huns. Expedito's life prior to his conversion would have been dissipated.
In Ancient Rome, soldiers were said to march expediti or in expeditionem when they did so only with their weapons and without cargo. On the contrary, they marched impediti whenever they did so with their impedimenta, a concept that included the sleeping bag, the eating utensils, the zapa tools, personal effects, supplies and tools.
In one of his hands he holds a palm leaf as a symbol of martyrdom and in the other a cross that displays the wordHodie, "Today" in Latin, as a tribute to the aforementioned legend. With his left foot he steps on a crow that is screaming"Cras", "Tomorrow" in Latin.
Although San Expedito is known worldwide for his extraordinary gift to solve the most urgent needs, he is also the Patron of Youth, Mediator in Trials and Proceedings, Student Relief, Health of the Sick and Protector in Family, Labor and Business, in addition to being able to be invoked in other cases.
"My Saint Expedito of the just and urgent causes, intercede for me together with Our Lord Jesus Christ, so that he may come to my aid in this hour of affliction and despair.
You who are the Saint of the afflicted, You who are the Saint of the desperate, You who are the Saint of urgent causes, protect me, help me, granting me: strength, courage and serenity.
Protect me from all who can harm me, protect my family.
Give me Peace and tranquility.
I will be grateful for the rest of my life and will spread your name to all who have Faith.
