WHERE ARE THEY USED?
If you've been wonderingWhat are units of measurement?
These units have been used for a long time, therefore, they have undergone some variations; due both to the needs of man, and to the advancement of technology. Thanks to this, even today we can find various units of measurement; here today, we will be talking about some of them.
We will start with measurements of mass, which are used to measure the amount that a body has. Mainly, the unit of mass is measured by means of grams; but, like many other units that we will see later, this one has multiples and submultiples.
Let's see it with some examples: the mass of a pear is approximately 2 hectograms, which if we put it in grams, would be 200 g; a spider has a mass of 1 g and a pencil has a mass of about 1 decagram.
It is important to point out that weight and mass should not be confused, since, although some measures of both are similar, these properties have different concepts; When we talk about weight, we mean the force that attracts a body through gravity, which will depend on its mass; For its part, we have already said that mass is the amount of matter that this body contains.
Well, very simple, through capacity units; which are used to calculate the amount of liquid that fits inside a container. The unit of capacity can also be found as a unit of volume, since capacity is precisely the volume that an object occupies in a given space.
; Well, the approximate capacity of a bottle of water is 1 liter. In the case of slightly larger objects; a barrel contains about 2 hl, as does a bathtub; on the other hand, an Olympic swimming pool has approximately 2500 kiloliters.
So far, we have talked about those units used to measure properties of objects, but what happens over time ?
3 months is a quarter.
Technology has advanced, and fields such as computing have become increasingly important in everyday life; Because of this, we are going to talk about storage units of measure in computing.
Surely you are interested in knowing what the natural numbers, here is the link to an article where you will learn everything about them
Next, we will tell you the parable of the pearl of great price, a story told by our Lord Jesus Christ. In addition, we will give you an interpretation of what this beautiful story could teach you to improve our lives.
Specifically, this parable of the pearl and the merchant (seller or merchant); We find it in the Gospel according to Matthew 13: 45-46. In these two verses, we find the following:
"That, having found a precious pearl, he went and sold everything he had, and bought it.
We can divide this story into 4 sections, to make it easier for you to read and better assimilate; the interpretation that you can give it is also as valid as the one we are going to say at the end of this article. However, we cannot forget the true teaching that Jesus wants to teach us with her.
Pearls are one of the most precious and precious stones that exist in the world; as notes, even in the time of Jesus, these stones were already quite valuable, so it is an excellent allegory to the Kingdom of Heaven. The merchant in question was always looking for the best pearls he could; since, he did not refrain from acquiring the first thing he saw.
Even when it seems that we achieve what we wanted so much, it is necessary to continue striving for it.
When being able to find the most precious pearl that the merchant has ever obtained, the merchant realizes that, to acquire it, he will have to pay a very high price; even one that exceeds your entire budget.
If you found this post interesting, we invite you to read our article on:God's creation.
Once decided, he gives absolutely everything he has in exchange for receiving the pearl in his hands; an object that, despite the fact that it made this man give everything he had; soon, it would bring you many more benefits and rewards than before. It can be assumed then, that the merchant did not really lose, but gained much more than he had given in return.
From this so beautiful parable, we can then get different interpretations with multiple teachings, even you can get yours. These teachings can be:
In order to receive something in return, it is necessary that we also give something in return and of the same value, of what we want to acquire; We cannot ask for something if we are not willing to do our best as well. However, despite this, we must act and give without expecting to receive something in return, because it is the right thing to do, to do from the heart.
These parables can be used on any occasion in daily life, be it to help or teach a person; Because, just as Jesus did with his followers, we also have the duty to teach and help others, especially those who need it most. That is the life of the good Catholic, the life of the good Christian.
In the gospels of the Bible, there will be many more parables, some of them not well known to most people.
