inquiry If you have any questions, be sure to leave messages for more information about cooling tower system and water treatment solutions.
Particles responsible for fouling of heat transfer surfaces are smaller than 5 microns. ICE high efficiency cooling tower water filters remove these extremely fine particles to provide the true benefits of clean cooling water.
ICE Industrial Reverse Osmosis System for Cooling Tower Water System
For industrial companies using a cooling tower for its facility, some type of cooling tower water treatment system is usually necessary to ensure an efficient process and longer equipment service life. If cooling tower water is left untreated, organic growth, fouling, scaling, and corrosion can r...
A cooling tower is a heat exchanger, inside of which heat is withdrawn from the water by contact between the water and the air. Cooling towers use water evaporation to reject heat from processes such as cooling the circulating water used in oil refineries, chemical plants, power plants, steel mil...
Industrial Reverse Osmosis System Buying Guide
3.Iron and manganese must be removed before the water enters reverse osmosis unit
ICE COOLING TOWER SYSTEM As your industrial cooling equipments and relevant associated water treatment solutions partner, we understand that the responsive and reliable after-sales services are critical for you, we'll work alongside with you throughout the full life cycle of your plant and equipment to ensure lasting business success.
For industrial companies using a cooling tower for its facility, some type of cooling tower water treatment system is usually necessary to ensure an efficient process and longer equipment service life. If cooling tower water is left untreated, organic growth, fouling, scaling, and corrosion can reduce plant productivity, cause plant downtime, and require costly equipment replacements down the road.
As mentioned above, the exact components of a cooling tower water treatment system depend on the quality of feed water and chemistry of circulatory water in relation to the quality of water needed for the specific cooling tower and related equipment(according to the manufacturer’s recommendations), but in general, a basic cooling tower water treatment system typically includes some type of:
Depending on the impurities present in the water, any combination of these treatments might best suit the facility and make up the treatment system, so it’s important to consult with the water treatment specialist to ensure the right system for the specific tower is being considered. Depending on the needs of the cooling tower and process, these standard components are usually adequate.
•alkalinity: will dictate potential of calcium carbonate scale
•hardness: contributes to scale in the cooling tower and on heat exchangers
•organic matter: promotes microorganism growth, which can lead to fouling, corrosion, and other system issues
•totals suspended solids (TSS):un-dissolved contaminants that can cause scaling, bio-films, and/or corrosion
Makeup water, or the water replacing bleed and evaporated and leaked water from the cooling tower, is first drawn from its source, which could be raw water, city water, city-treated effluent, in-plant wastewater recycle, well water, or any other surface water source.
At this point of the process, the proper treatment optimizes the tower evaporation cycles and minimizes the water bleed rate to drain beyond what might be done with chemicals alone. Filtration and ultra-filtration
