The setting of the multi-SSID function is very simple, we only need to log in to the web configuration interface of the 4G router, find the “wireless setting” menu, and then enter multiple wireless network names. In order to ensure that your own wireless LAN is not illegally “invaded” by others, you can set wireless encryption for each SSID (all SSID encryption methods must be the same, and the names can be inconsistent).
Because the signal coverage of a 4G router is limited, if you want to use the multi-SSID function of the wireless router, its application area should not exceed 200 square meters.
There are also certain requirements for the original network bandwidth. If the bandwidth is too low (<2M) or there are too many wireless clients (>20), it is not recommended to use this function.
This group is often lower than the average bandwidth allocated by the previous groups of SSIDs, so in actual applications, we must pay attention to this point and try not to use the last group of SSIDs.
