NEWS>Possible factors for the low wireless negotiation rate of 4G routers
After the wireless terminal is connected to the wireless signal of the 4G router, the wireless rate displayed on the terminal is lower, as shown in the figure below.
In general, the highest wireless rate of mobile phones and other terminals in the 2.4G frequency band is 72Mbps (150Mbps in some cases), and the negotiated wireless rate is lower after connecting with a 4G router.
If you modify the wireless mode to 11bg mixed, 11g only, 11b only, or modify the frequency band bandwidth to 20MHz, it will affect the maximum wireless rate of the 4G router signal. Please keep the default setting (40MHz).
In Wireless Settings >> Wireless Advanced Settings, if you do not check to enable WMM, the router is working in 11g mode, and the wireless rate is 54Mbps. The maximum negotiated rate for wireless terminals connecting to the router is 54Mbps.
Wireless interference In the use environment of a 4G router or wireless terminal, if there are many other wireless signals, they will interfere with each other, which will affect the negotiation rate of the wireless terminal or cause the wireless negotiation rate to be unstable.
