Data map: Operators start network frequency reduction.
A few days ago, it was reported that the Fuzhou Municipal Radio Administration Bureau sent a letter to Fuzhou Mobile, “Your organization’s report on the application for cancellation of TD-SCDMA base stations has been received. After research, it has been agreed to cancel the 6535 TD-SCDMA base stations that your organization has stopped using.
Does the 4G gateway affect the normal use of users?
Independent telecom analyst Fu Liang believes that the frequency reduction of the three major operators’ networks is a gradual process, and 2G users don’t need to worry too much. China Unicom also said before that frequency reduction is not about shutting down the network, but a process of gradual “slimming”.
As for why it has to withdraw from the network, Xiang Ligang said, TD-SCDMA, like other 3G and 4G technologies, has its main function as data services, 4G gateway but 3G technology, a base station only supports about 20M traffic, which is very weak. In addition, leaving the network is for efficient use of spectrum.
The operators themselves admit this. In April 2018, China Unicom issued an announcement that the 4G gateway stated that it is proceeding in an orderly manner with frequency reduction for 2G networks.
It can be seen that frequency bands are so precious, no wonder operators want to re-cultivation frequency bands. So, what kind of user are you and will you try 5G?
