The Rural Energy for America Program, or REAP, is a federal grant program that provides funding to agricultural producers and rural small businesses for renewable energy and energy efficiency projects. The Massachusetts Farm Energy Program is able to provide free assistance to farms and rural small businesses throughout Massachusetts who are interested in applying to this grant.
The REAP Application Overview webinar will provide an outline of REAP grant guidelines and application requirements, while the Demystifying DUNS & SAM webinar will walk through the processes for obtaining these numbers step by step. There will be time after each webinar for attendees to obtain individual help, and both webinars can also be attended in person at EcoBuilding Bargains (83 Warwick St. Springfield).
