The EPA estimated that around 600 million tons of construction and demolition materials were thrown away in the U.S. in 2018. These discarded materials come from building demolitions and renovations and their total weight is more than double that of all other yearly U.S. municipal solid waste.
As a result, deconstruction can sometimes be less expensive opens PDF file than demolition after tax deductions. Not only does this help tax payers, but deconstructed materials are then sold at a discounted price, which can help lower income homeowners in their home projects.
