HERS Rating FAQ - Center for EcoTechnology Skip to content
HERS ratings are required for new construction projects and major renovations in any of the over 278 municipalities opens PDF file in Massachusetts that have adopted the stretch energy code. The HERS Index is a number that tells homeowners and home-buyers how energy efficient a home is, and how much they should expect to spend on heating and cooling costs.
How is the HERS rating of my home calculated?
Your HERS rating is calculated by a home energy rater, like the HERS-trained high-performance building experts at the Center for EcoTechnology. They perform an extensive examination of the home and use a computer model to generate your HERS rating.
What are some other benefits of HERS ratings?
Getting a HERS rating can help you understand the energy performance of your new home, and where you can make the most efficient upgrades in order to reduce energy consumption, making your living space more comfortable and more affordable to heat and cool!
