This represents more than double the amount of everyday garbage discarded by the public in the U.S. annually. A great way to reduce this waste is through deconstruction, which keeps perfectly good building materials and appliances out of landfills and can lower construction and remodeling costs for homeowners with reduced disposal fees and possible tax deductions.
