Educate yourself. Do you know what objects are and are not recyclable in your area?
Don’t wishcycle. “Wishcycling” or “wishful recycling” refers to a consumer’s tendency to put something in their recycling bins because they believe it should be recycled even if it is not on the list of approved materials for the local MRF.
Think reusable- whether it’s water bottles, forks and knives, food storage containers, towels, etc., do everything you can to avoid using disposable options. When possible, buy in bulk- a single two-liter soda bottle is less wasteful than a 12-pack of smaller bottles.
